--- At Pythagorean q (sanity check) ---
  q = 4/3:  N = 21
  Emin = [1, 0, 0, -4, -1]

=== Conclusions on Tate types ===
Direct symbolic Delta = 16 q^4 (q-1)^2 (q+1)^2 tells us:
  v_q(Delta) at q=0: 4. v_q(c4): 0. ==> I_4 (mult).
  v_q(Delta) at q=1: 2. v_q(c4): 0. ==> I_2 (mult).
  Similarly at q=-1, infty.

Shioda-Tate:
  rho(V') = 2 + r_gen + (4-1) + (4-1) + (2-1) + (2-1)
         = 10 + r_gen.

Frobenius traces (from picard_frobenius.gp):
  trace_p/p at p=7 is 6 ==> rho_geom >= 6.
  Lower bound 10 from Shioda-Tate dominates.

Conclusion: rho(V') >= 10. With r_gen = 0, rho = 10.
